    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "There are n train stops between Chennai and Assam. How many train tickets are to\nbe printed, so that a person can travel between any of the two stations (irrespective of\ndirection of travel)?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "(n+2)*(n+1)/2",
        "(n+2)(n+1)/2"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "There are n+2 stations, including both endpoints. Each unordered pair needs one ticket when direction is ignored."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "A man desires to throw a party for some of his friends. In how many ways can he\nselect m friends from a group of n friends, if the two of his friends (say ’A’ and ’B’)\nwill not attend the party together?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "binom(n,m)-binom(n-2,m-2)"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Subtract selections containing both A and B from all selections of m friends."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Suman has m clothes of different types, say, C1, C2, ..., Cm and she wants to wear all\nthese clothes at different days, say, D1, D2, ..., Dm. Due to some reason,C1 must be\nused either at Dm−2 or at Dm−1 and C2 can be used either at Dm−1 or at Dm−2 and\nat Dm. Every cloth is to be used at only one day, In how many ways can clothes be\nused?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "4*(m-2)!",
        "4(m-2)!"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "There are 2 choices for the day of C1 and then 2 admissible choices for C2. Arrange all remaining clothes freely."
        }
      ]
    },
